{#
sharing/booked.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The page after a booking went through.

A page of its own rather than a banner on the form, and the reason is the
unique constraint: leaving a filled-in form on screen invites a second submit,
which the database would refuse correctly and inexplicably ("that time has just
been taken" — by yourself, a second ago). Replacing the form removes the
temptation entirely.

It deliberately does NOT repeat the time. The confirmation mail carries it, in
the booker's own zone and with an .ics attached, and a page saying "10:30" in
whichever clock the browser happened to be reading is one more chance for the
two to disagree. What this page promises is exactly what has happened: the
appointment is made and a message is on its way.

Variables:
  page        BookingPage       what was booked, for the heading
  appearance  PublicAppearance  the owner's theme, so this page and the form
                                that led to it are visibly the same place
#}
{% extends 'sharing/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'calendar.booking.booked.title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <div class="rounded-pane border border-line bg-surface px-6 py-10 text-center">
        <span class="mx-auto w-12 h-12 flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent"
              aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-check text-xl"></i></span>

        <h1 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'calendar.booking.booked.title'|trans }}</h1>

        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">
            {{ 'calendar.booking.booked.body'|trans({ '%name%': page.name }) }}
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-faint">{{ 'calendar.booking.booked.mail'|trans }}</p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
